.TH CLEAR 1
.SH NAME
clear \- clear the terminal screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clear
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clear
clears the screen of the terminal, if it can be cleared, and puts the
cursor at the top left. It finds the terminal's type in the environment
variable TERM, and how to clear its screen, the
.B cl
capability, in the terminal capability data base,
.BR /etc/termcap .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP 10
.B TERM
the type of the terminal
.TP
.B TERMCAP
another termcap file to read, if it begins with /, or the terminal's
entry itself (see
.BR termcap (3))
.SH FILES
.TP 14
/etc/termcap
the terminal capability data base
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
"TERM is not set", "cannot read /etc/termcap", "unknown terminal type",
or "a
.I type
cannot clear its screen" when the entry has no cl capability. The exit
status is 1 when the screen was not cleared.
.SH SEE ALSO
termcap(3), tset(1)
.SH HISTORY
A
.B clear
command using the termcap data base and library appeared in 2BSD, in
1979.
.SH AUTHORS
This clear was written for the xenix86-devsys Development System.
